15.1 Law and forum. Tennessee law and applicable United States federal law govern, without using a choice-of-law rule to displace that selection. To the extent enforceable, federal copyright or patent claims under this license must proceed in the United States District Court for the Middle District of Tennessee, Nashville Division, when it has subject-matter jurisdiction and legally proper venue. Other disputes under this license must proceed in the state courts sitting in Dickson County, Tennessee, or that federal court when it has jurisdiction and proper venue. If mandatory jurisdiction or venue rules preclude those courts, an otherwise competent court with legally proper venue may hear the claim. The parties consent to personal jurisdiction to the extent enforceable.

This section does not limit where Licensor may bring a claim against a person who has not accepted this license, or seek interim injunctive relief against ongoing infringement or misuse of Covered Material in a court of competent jurisdiction. It does not establish jurisdiction or venue by itself, establish entitlement to an injunction, override mandatory consumer protections or other nonwaivable rules, or require arbitration or a class-action waiver.

