A notice must be durable written communication identifying the sender, intended recipient, relevant release or agreement, provision and alleged conduct or requested action. Notices from Licensor to You must be directed to a contact address You have designated or otherwise provided for relevant communications, or another address/channel through which actual receipt or legally effective delivery to You can be established. They need not be sent to Licensor's own mailbox. A public account, repository or commit contact may help identify a delivery route only after Licensor or an authorized representative reasonably verifies, using documented evidence, that the route is associated with the intended recipient. That verification does not, by itself, establish receipt or legally effective delivery. No user registration or publication of a personal address is required merely to use ChezCat.

A contractual notice is effective when receipt by the intended recipient is established, or at another time required by applicable law. Receipt does not necessarily require a personal reply, but sending an email, receiving no bounce, or posting a public issue does not alone conclusively establish receipt. Retain reasonable delivery evidence. The correction period in Section 11.2 runs from the recipient's receipt of the written violation notice, not from its public posting or the sender's intention to send it. Difficulty delivering notice does not grant permission for unauthorized conduct or, by itself, postpone the operation of Section 11.1; it can prevent the notice-based reinstatement period from starting. An express signed agreement can specify additional lawful notice mechanics for that agreement.

Contractual notice is not automatically service of process. Court service, statutory notices and other legally prescribed procedures must satisfy the applicable requirements. Do not send confidential security findings to a public issue; follow Section 8.3 and SECURITY.md.

